:: Retail Pitch [event main_quest] {"position":"5825,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Retail Pitch" (main_retailPitch), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.11, second half. The night before the biggest pitch we've
   ever had, the demo for $retailChain.name. I ask $ethan.name to set up the demo equipment overnight and give him master access
   to everything, because tonight there's nobody else who can do it. Later, at home, I have the office camera open on my phone
   and almost check on him. The choice sets $flags.trustedEthan:
     true   I leave the footage alone
     false  I watch: he's doing exactly what I asked, and I feel a little stupid
   A line changes with how we got the introduction ($flags.retailIntro: "broker", "wait" or "sister").
   The pitch itself is tomorrow, off screen. The scene ends at home, Late Night. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[13].img>><</silent>>
<<if $flags.retailIntro === "sister">>
Tomorrow at ten, four people from $retailChain.name are coming up to our meeting room, because $investor.callName asked them to, because of a rooftop evening $sister.callName still hasn't really told me about.
<<elseif $flags.retailIntro === "broker">>
Tomorrow at ten, four people from $retailChain.name are coming up to our meeting room. The introduction cost more than $mom.callName's car is worth, paid to a man who made two phone calls and charged by the minute for both.
<<else>>
Tomorrow at ten, four people from $retailChain.name are coming up to our meeting room. I waited two weeks for $investor.callName to make the call he could have made in an afternoon, and I've been checking my phone every hour since.
<</if>>

Four hundred stores. Eleven hundred conference rooms, give or take, according to $darius.name, who counted. If tomorrow goes well, we stop being a startup and become a supplier.

Everything has to work. Three Veil units on stands in the meeting room, a live readout on the big screen showing the room settle in real time, $darius.name's charts, a short video $sister.callName cut together from the gym installations. All of it has to be set up, tested, and tested again tonight, so that tomorrow nobody touches a single cable.

<<linkreplace "Find $ethan.name">>
He's in the meeting room already, on his knees under the table, feeding a cable through a hole in the floor with his tongue between his teeth.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "If you're here to supervise, I accept tips in the form of pizza." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm here to ask you a favor." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Then I accept tips in the form of extra pizza." },
{ text: "He crawls out from under the table and sits back on his heels, dusting off his hands." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I need you to stay tonight and finish the setup. All of it. Units, readout, the screen, the network. Test everything twice. I need to be home and asleep, or I'll walk in there tomorrow looking like a raccoon." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "You always look like a raccoon. It's part of your charm." },
{ who: $player, text: "And you'll need this." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Give him master access">>
I hand him a sticky note with a password on it, written in my own handwriting, because I don't want it in a message anywhere. It opens the password vault. The vault opens everything else: the servers, the device configs, the building's access system, the camera feeds, the admin panel for the units. Including the one in the ceiling.

He looks at the sticky note for a moment without taking it.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $ethan, text: "Master access." },
{ who: $player, text: "For tonight. If something breaks at three in the morning, I don't want you waiting on me to unlock it." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "The keys to the kingdom." },
{ who: $player, text: "The keys to a meeting room and four hundred stores." },
{ text: "He takes it. He folds it once and puts it in his shirt pocket, behind his pen, and taps the pocket." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "I'll take good care of it, boss. Go home. Sleep. Dream about four hundred stores." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I watch him crawl back under the table. He's humming. Out in the main office, behind the vent, the unit he has never seen hums along with him.

<div class="navigation-link"><<link "Go home" "Retail Pitch 2">><<AdvanceTimeTo 6>><</link>></div>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>


:: Retail Pitch 2 [event main_quest] {"position":"5950,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Retail Pitch" (main_retailPitch), part 2 of 2: that night at home, the office camera on my phone. The choice
   sets $flags.trustedEthan and finishes the quest. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[1].img>><</silent>>
I don't sleep.

At half past one I'm lying in the dark with my phone on my chest, and the camera app is open. One tap, and I'd see the meeting room, or the main office, or the server corner. I'd see exactly what he's doing with the keys to everything I own.

There's no reason to. He's setting up a demo. He's done a hundred setups. He has never once given me a reason.

My thumb is over the button anyway.

/* MEDIA: images/events/retail_pitch/phone.jpg | His face in the dark, lit by a phone screen showing a grid of camera thumbnails */

<div id="rp-choice">
<div>
<<link "Leave the footage alone">><<replace "#rp-choice">>
I lock the phone and put it face down on the nightstand.

He's my friend. He's been my friend since a hackathon at four in the morning with a bike helmet full of wires. He's the guy who told me not to tell him what the dial does. If I start watching him through the ceiling the night before the most important day of the company's life, I don't really have a friend. I just have one more person I keep an eye on.

So I don't. I lie there and listen to the house, and at some point I fall asleep.

<<set $flags.trustedEthan to true>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent "Sleep" "Bedroom">>
<</replace>><</link>>
</div>
<div>
<<link "Check the footage">><<replace "#rp-choice">>
I tap it.

The meeting room, from the corner camera, grainy and green. The three units are on their stands. The screen is on, showing the readout: a calm blue line across the bottom. $ethan.name is sitting at the head of the table with his laptop and a cold slice of pizza, typing, with his headphones on. As I watch, he gets up, walks to the middle unit, adjusts its angle by a centimeter, walks back, checks the readout and nods to himself.

I switch to the main office. Empty. The server corner. Empty, the lights blinking the way they always blink.

Back to the meeting room. He's on the floor under the table again, taping down a cable so nobody trips on it tomorrow. He tapes it twice.

I watch for twenty minutes. He doesn't do a single thing I didn't ask him to do.

I close the app feeling like I've read somebody's diary and found nothing in it but grocery lists. It isn't a good feeling or a bad one, just one more thing I know that he doesn't know I know.

<<set $flags.trustedEthan to false>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent "Sleep" "Bedroom">>
<</replace>><</link>>
</div>
</div>
